{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":502204,"name":"Wes Anderson","username":"Wes_Anderson","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/w/0ea827/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-27T18:42:59.156Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502204-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502204-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502204-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502204-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn Grok Bot, the Gmail connector can’t see or act on messages in the Spam folder. When I asked my assistant to delete the spam in our support inbox, it searched and reported the folder as empty. Gmail itself showed 9 messages in Spam for the same account. Searches with in:spam, label:SPAM, and in:anywhere all return an empty result, even when searching for an exact sender that’s sitting in Spam. Search works normally for the inbox and all other folders. Because the empty result looks like “no mail,” the assistant gave me wrong information\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502204-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502204-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eConnect a Gmail account to a Grok Bot assistant through the Gmail connector.\u003cbr\u003e\nMake sure the account has messages in Spam (confirm in the Gmail web app).\u003cbr\u003e\nAsk the assistant to list or delete the messages in Spam.\u003cbr\u003e\nThe connector’s search comes back empty for in:spam, label:SPAM, and in:anywhere, so the assistant can’t find or delete them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502204-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502204-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe connector should be able to list Spam messages and trash or delete them, perhaps through an includeSpam option like the existing includeTrash. At minimum, it should return a clear message that Spam is excluded, not an empty result that looks like “there’s nothing here.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502204-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502204-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502204-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502204-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot 0.61.0\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502204-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502204-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: which model did you use?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502204-for-ai-issues-add-request-id-with-privacy-disabled-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502204-for-ai-issues-add-request-id-with-privacy-disabled-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: add Request ID with privacy disabled\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eN/A\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502204-additional-information-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502204-additional-information-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis happened on Sunday, Sep 27, 2026, around 12:30 PM CT, in a Grok Bot assistant connected to a Google Workspace Gmail account. The same connector finds messages in the Inbox, Sent, Drafts, and custom labels without trouble, and it can see Trash when its includeTrash option is turned on. Only Spam is invisible. Even a message we had given our own “Vendor pitch” label disappeared from search once Gmail moved it into Spam. What makes it confusing is that an empty result looks the same as “nothing here,” so the assistant told me my Spam folder was empty when it had 9 messages in it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-502204-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-10\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-502204-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-10\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSometimes - I can sometimes use Cursor\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-27T18:43:05.706Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":5,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":25.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":173140,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-gmail-connector-cant-see-the-spam-folder-searches-return-empty","display_username":"Wes Anderson","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136160,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-gmail-connector-cant-see-the-spam-folder-searches-return-empty/173140/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":502246,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png